00:43:32.960 --> 00:43:50.670
<v Ira Glass>It's This American Life. I'm Ira Glass. Today's program, watching the watchers, people deciding on their own that it is their job to make sure that bad things don't happen, and then beginning their own surveillance of suspected wrongdoers. We have arrived at Act 2 of our show. Act 2, I'll Be Watching You.
<v Ira Glass>这里是《美国生活》。我是艾拉·格拉斯。今天的节目，监视监视者，人们自己决定他们的工作是确保坏事不会发生，然后开始对自己怀疑的作恶者进行监视。我们已经来到了节目的第二幕。第二幕，《我会监视你》。

00:43:50.670 --> 00:44:05.140
<v Ira Glass>Sixth grade isn't that old, but it's old enough to tell right from wrong. And it's old enough to know that adults aren't always perfect. And at Davisville Middle School in Rhode Island, this one sixth grader couldn't help but notice that one of his teachers was doing stuff that just felt a little weird.
<v Ira Glass>六年级还没那么大，但足以分辨是非。足以知道成年人并不总是完美的。在罗德岛州的戴维斯维尔中学，这位六年级学生忍不住注意到他的一位老师做的事情看起来有点怪。

00:44:05.140 --> 00:44:14.860
<v Ira Glass>Much, much later, the teacher would be removed from the school for his behavior. But at this stage, early on, this sixth grader was seeing certain things for the first time. Like at Halloween.
<v Ira Glass>很久很久以后，那位老师因为他的行为被学校开除了。但在早期阶段，这位六年级学生第一次看到了一些特定的事情。比如在万圣节。

00:44:14.860 --> 00:44:21.370
<v Student>He was making remarks about some of the girls' costumes and makeup that were coming off as creepy and flirtatious.
<v Student>他会对一些女生的服装和妆容发表评论，这些话听起来令人毛骨悚然且轻浮。

00:44:21.370 --> 00:44:22.630
<v Ira Glass>What did he say?
