00:44:34.060 --> 00:44:48.730
<v Student>He was just-- he was just getting in closer, and he was kind of leaning in a way where it looked-- it just seemed creepy. Something seemed off about it. You could just sense it. I don't know. It seemed like she was uncomfortable by it. Like, nervously laughing at it.
<v Student>他只是——他只是靠得更近了，他倾身的方式看起来——这只是显得很诡异。感觉有点不对劲。你就是能感觉到。我不知道。看起来她对此很不舒服。就像在紧张地笑着一样。

00:44:48.730 --> 00:45:04.690
<v Ira Glass>Every time this teacher did other things, he says, the kinds of stuff the kids notice, he asked a girl to take off her shoe and wiggle her toes for him, made an unsettling joke about how everybody should come to school in their bathing suits, and as the school year continued, that one girl from Halloween was a special target.
<v Ira Glass>他说，每次这名老师做其他事情时，都是那种孩子们会注意到的事情，他要求一个女孩脱掉鞋子为他动动脚趾，还开了个令人不安的玩笑，说每个人都应该穿泳衣来学校，随着学年继续，万圣节时那个女孩成了特别的目标。

00:45:04.690 --> 00:45:27.190
<v Student>And I would remember him always stopping the class to make remarks about her or her appearance, or calling her pet names, making a play on her name. Put it in nursery rhymes or songs. He just started conversation with her individually in front of the whole class, like talking about stuff that was not related to class, just to make her laugh.
<v Student>我会记得他总是停下课堂对她或她的外表发表评论，或者给她起昵称，玩弄她的名字。把它编进童谣或歌曲里。他只是在全班同学面前和她开始单独对话，比如谈论和课堂无关的事情，只是为了让她笑。

00:45:27.190 --> 00:45:43.980
<v Student>You can notice she's nervously laughing or blushing at it. Other kids in the class were weirded out by it. Everybody sits there in awkward silence as you do that.
<v Student>你可以注意到她对此紧张地笑着或脸红。班上的其他孩子对此感到很古怪。当你这样做时，每个人都坐在那里陷入尴尬的沉默。

00:45:43.980 --> 00:45:47.070
<v Ira Glass>Did you ever talk to her about it?
<v Ira Glass>你有跟她谈过这件事吗？

00:45:47.070 --> 00:45:53.400
