<v Student>We just did it. Yeah, we just did it because the name was funny.
<v Student>我们只是做了。是的，我们只是做了，因为这个名字很有趣。

00:48:00.090 --> 00:48:13.590
<v Ira Glass>To be clear, he knows he's using the word pedo loosely. The Pedo Database was an inside joke between a small group of boys who hated this teacher because he was so harsh with them. But they were also totally serious about the way he was treating the girls.
<v Ira Glass>需要明确的是，他知道自己是在随意使用“恋童癖”这个词。“恋童癖数据库”是那一小群讨厌老师的男孩之间的内部笑话，因为他对他们太苛刻了。但他们对老师对待女孩的方式也是完全认真的。

00:48:13.590 --> 00:48:22.020
<v Ira Glass>And is the idea that you think you might accumulate enough evidence that you guys will go to the authorities at some point?
<v Ira Glass>你们的想法是，积累足够的证据，以便将来去向当局报告吗？

00:48:22.020 --> 00:48:42.790
<v Student>I don't know what that was. I mean, in my log, we just said this is now the official chat that we will later use as evidence against him about pedophilia. That's the word I used, in case anything does come up in the future and we do turn out to be correct. And I said, whenever he said something creepy towards the girls in our class, posting quotes with the date here.
<v Student>我不知道那是什么。我的意思是，在我的日志里，我们只是说这是我们以后用来作为针对他恋童癖证据的官方聊天记录。“恋童癖”是我用的词，以防将来发生什么事情，而我们最终证明是正确的。我说，每当他对我们班的女孩说些诡异的话时，就在这里贴上带日期的引用。

00:48:42.790 --> 00:48:46.450
<v Ira Glass>Logging the date was actually something they got from watching TV and movies, true crime.
