00:49:30.740 --> 00:49:46.480
<v Ira Glass>And every few weeks, the teacher did something noteworthy enough that one of the boys would jot it down on a pad secretly, right then in class, or type it directly into Discord on his phone, adding an entry to the database log. These kids finished with that teacher, moved on to the next teacher.
<v Ira Glass>每隔几周，老师就会做一些值得注意的事情，以至于其中一个男孩会偷偷地记在纸上，就在课上，或者直接输入到Discord手机里，在数据库日志中增加一个条目。这些孩子在那位老师的课上结束了，转到了下一个老师的班级。

00:49:46.480 --> 00:49:52.270
<v Ira Glass>But to keep the log going, they enlisted kids who had him the next year. And they read the new entries.
<v Ira Glass>但为了让日志继续下去，他们拉拢了下一年有那个老师的学生。他们阅读新的条目。

00:49:52.270 --> 00:50:05.020
<v Student>It's not like we wanted him to say bad things, but it was satisfying when we did, because then we'd be like, all right, great, another piece for the record. Every time he said something, it's like we pictured him punching himself in the face.
<v Student>并不是说我们希望他说坏话，但当他说的时候这让人满足，因为那样我们就想，好吧，太棒了，记录里又多了一条。每次他说什么，我们就像看到他在给自己脸上打了一拳。

00:50:05.020 --> 00:50:10.930
<v Ira Glass>It's interesting to me that it was all boys doing this. I would think that girls would have wanted to get in on it, if they knew it existed.
<v Ira Glass>让我感兴趣的是，全都是男孩在做这个。如果女孩们知道它存在的话，我觉得她们也会想加入进来。

00:50:10.930 --> 00:50:18.040
<v Student>Perhaps they would have, but we didn't bring it up. But I'm sure maybe some of them would. We just didn't really have any girls in our friend group.
