00:50:18.040 --> 00:50:20.800
<v Ira Glass>Oh, right. Right. Middle school.
<v Ira Glass>噢，对了。对了。初中。

00:50:20.800 --> 00:50:27.160
<v Student>Yes, exactly.
<v Student>是的，完全正确。

00:50:27.160 --> 00:50:53.450
<v Ira Glass>The reporter who broke this story and revealed the Pedo Database to the world is Amanda Milkovits of the Boston Globe. And the reason it became public, the reason she wrote a story is that in April of this year, the teacher was removed from his job and put on leave because of allegations that he'd stalked a girl, a pre-teen at the school. After that happened, there was a public appeal to families in the school for any information about other incidents involving this teacher.
<v Ira Glass>揭露了这个故事并将“恋童癖数据库”展示给世界的记者是《波士顿环球报》的阿曼达·米尔科维茨。它之所以公开，她写这个故事的原因是，在今年4月，这位老师因为被指控跟踪一名女生、学校的一名青春期前女孩而被停职。在那之后，学校公开呼吁家庭提供关于涉及这位老师的其他事件的任何信息。

00:50:53.450 --> 00:51:07.460
<v Student>And my mom told me about it. And I told her, oh, well, we have this whole log my friends and I compiled. I was actually shocked. I mean, it was almost like we predicted the future when I was like, oh my god, I could-- it all paid off.
<v Student>我妈妈告诉了我。我告诉她，噢，我们有这本我和朋友汇编的完整日志。我当时真的很震惊。我的意思是，这几乎就像我们预言了未来，当我说，噢我的天，我可以——一切都得到了回报。

00:51:07.460 --> 00:51:11.960
<v Ira Glass>Did you have this feeling of like, I can't believe this is happening, I can't believe that we get to use this thing?
